SECTION 1: DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Base Open-Source Components": Standard foundational markup, raw ECMA-compliant script primitives, universal W3C specifications, and third-party libraries governed independently by MIT, Apache-2.0, or BSD-3-Clause licenses.  
1.2 "Direct Clone Bundle": Contiguous file-tree reproduction, git-managed duplication, serialized folder extraction, or component glue-code replication that preserves the proprietary architectural arrangement, JSON/YAML manifest structures, and token cascading unique to the Licensors.  
1.3 "Clean-Room Reimplementation": Independent cognitive derivation, manual keystroke transcription into an independent repository sharing zero byte-level or structural file-tree lineage, derived solely from visual inspection of public-facing renders.  
1.4 "Stipulated Fee": The mandatory financial consideration defined in Section 3.1.  

---

SECTION 2: LICENSE GRANT & DUAL-TIER BIFURCATION

2.1 The Clean-Room Free Tier
Any individual may ocularly inspect public renderings, commit architectural patterns to memory, and manually author an independent, clean-room implementation free of charge, subject to strict prohibition against automated scraping, bulk tarball extraction, or direct git-tree mirroring exceeding 14 contiguous lines of proprietary component glue.

2.2 The Direct Clone Commercial Grant
Upon satisfaction of Section 3, Licensors grant Licensee a non-exclusive, worldwide, perpetual right to utilize, modify, and deploy the Direct Clone Bundle for personal, staging, internal, or commercial production workloads. Redistribution of the raw Direct Clone Bundle as a competing UI template marketplace product remains strictly prohibited.

